 Recommendations from within Claude Code team on Session Management - comma=
nds =F0=9F=9A=80<br><br><br>/usage - lists down the usage plan limits and r=
ate limits. Available natively as a button in Claude Desktop App. Not on De=
sktop App? Try setting up Status lines in CLI<br><br>/rewind - resets to a =
previous checkpoint in the chat. Use when you want to say =E2=80=9CNo, that=
=E2=80=99s not what I meant=E2=80=A6=E2=80=9D Additionaly allows summarizat=
ion of the change of course to be used by Claude. Rewind is the preferred o=
ption to disagree with Claude Code<br><br>/clear - clears the context to fr=
esh slate, just like it was when you opened Claude Code<br><br>/compact - c=
ompacts the contents in the context into one liners. Useful inside a long r=
unning session. Or passing info from one step of an activity to the next in=
side the same session<br><br>=E2=9D=A4=EF=B8=8F /rewind is my favourite in =
the list. There=E2=80=99s always disagreement with Claude. It=E2=80=99s a m=
ess to keep conflicting sentences in Claude=E2=80=99s memory and expect Cla=
ude to pick the right one. Claude Code recommends using rewind command. Rew=
ind command removes the traces of wandering from Context so Claude can avoi=
d mistakes. <br><br>You have 3 options when using Rewind. 3rd option is =E2=
=80=9CI don=E2=80=99t care=E2=80=9D. First option totally ignores the direc=
tion Claude Code took and restores to a previous point in the conversation =
by forking the conversation. Every turn is tracked. You don=E2=80=99t need =
to do anything special to save a restoration point. The second option resto=
res to a point in the conversation, and additionally summarises all the mes=
sages after that restoration point - much like teaching Claude what happene=
d afterwards but you didn=E2=80=99t like. <br><br>/usage command is built-i=
n to the Desktop app. At the footer next to the Model and Effort, there is =
a new pie icon which pops open a small floating window. This window capture=
s rates and limits. If you are on CLI try setting status lines in Claude <b=
r><br>=F0=9F=94=97 Expected a hyperlink to the doc? No, try asking Claude t=
